<section class="hero-wrapper">

  <div class="hero-left">
    <span class="greeting anim-rise delay-1">Hi, I'm Adithya.</span>
    <h1 class="anim-rise delay-2">I put machine learning on tiny chips, teach computing from first principles, and <em>write through what I'm learning.</em></h1>
    <div class="hero-body anim-rise delay-3">
      <p>
        I'm an embedded ML systems engineer in Bengaluru, working on Edge AI and
        TinyML at IISc's NeuRonICS Lab &mdash; machine learning that runs on
        microcontrollers with kilobytes of memory, across audio, radar, and
        event-based vision. Before that I co-founded a company building a moisture
        meter for the cashew industry, in the field since 2021. Along the way I've
        taught at IISc, on NPTEL, and at TalentSprint, and I currently teach
        computer organisation and architecture.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is where all of that lands: a project log, a classroom, and a
        notebook. A lot of it is work-in-progress. Some of it turns out to be
        wrong on the first try. I update things as I learn better.
      </p>
      <div class="ai-callout">
        <strong>Fair warning:</strong> I use AI to help write and structure many of
        the notes here. The ideas, the projects, and the learning are mine; the
        words often get a pass through an LLM first. I'd rather say that plainly
        than pretend otherwise.
      </div>
    </div>
